## Why This Is Asked

This question tests multi-account Terraform patterns: provider aliases, cross-account data sources, and deterministic apply order.

## Key Concepts

- Aliased providers
- Cross-account data sources
- Data referencing across providers
- depends_on for ordering
- Credentials management via profiles and assume_role

## Code Example

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  alias   = "prod"
  region  = "us-east-1"
  profile = "prod"
}
provider "aws" {
  alias   = "audit"
  region  = "us-east-1"
  profile = "audit"
}

data "aws_caller_identity" "prod" {
  provider = aws.prod
}

data "aws_s3_bucket" "prod_bucket" {
  provider = aws.prod
  bucket   = "my-prod-bucket"
}

data "aws_iam_policy_document" "audit" {
  provider = aws.audit
  statement {
    actions   = ["s3:GetObject"]
    resources = ["${data.aws_s3_bucket.prod_bucket.arn}/*"]
    principals {
      type        = "AWS"
      identifiers = ["arn:aws:iam::${data.aws_caller_identity.prod.account_id}:root"]
    }
  }
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket" "audit_bucket" {
  provider = aws.audit
  bucket   = "audit-bucket"
}

resource "aws_iam_policy" "audit_policy" {
  provider = aws.audit
  name     = "CrossAccountGetObject"
  policy   = data.aws_iam_policy_document.audit.json
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you rotate credentials for the aliased providers safely?
- How would you test this cross-account permission in a CI workflow?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of remote state isolation, cross-env data sharing, and basic CI gating for beginner Terraform workflows.

## Key Concepts
- terraform_remote_state data source
- backend alias and per-env state keys
- var-files for environment specificity (qa.tfvars)
- CI gating with plan validation before apply

## Code Example
```javascript
// qa backend example (HCL in Terraform syntax, shown as JS for formatting)
terraform {
  backend "s3" {
    bucket         = "my-terraform-state"
    key            = "envs/qa/terraform.tfstate"
    region         = "us-east-1"
    dynamodb_table = "tf-locks"
  }
}

data "terraform_remote_state" "prod" {
  backend = "s3"
  config = {
    bucket = "my-terraform-state"
    key    = "envs/prod/terraform.tfstate"
    region = "us-east-1"
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you extend this to multi-region VPCs?
- How would you test for drift between prod and qa after apply?
